From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: run the H713 video engine at 432 MHz

The H713's AV1 decoder is a separate core (a Google IP at 0x01c0d000,
driven by hantro's H713 variant), but it runs from the video engine's
module clock. At the 600 MHz the H6 variant asks for, the AV1 core stalls
into its own cycle timeout on every frame; at 432 MHz -- what the stock
firmware programs -- the same frame decodes bit-exact. Measured by
replaying a vendor register image with PLL_VE at each rate, 2026-09-29.

The H713 binds the H6 compatible, so it is recognised by machine, as the
polyphase and VP9 capabilities already are. Cedrus loses 28% of its clock
on this SoC; the panel it drives is 1280x720.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0144-media-cedrus-run-the-h713-video-engine-at-432-mhz.patch (0144-media-cedrus-run-the-h713-video-engine-at-432-mhz.patch, commit 46bc559)
---
diff --color -Naur pa/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c pb/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -628,7 +628,14 @@
 		goto err_sram;
 	}
 
-	ret = clk_set_rate(dev->mod_clk, variant->mod_rate);
+	/*
+	 * The H713's AV1 decoder, a separate core, runs from this same module
+	 * clock and stalls into its own timeout above 432 MHz, so the H713 VE
+	 * runs there rather than at the H6's 600 MHz.
+	 */
+	ret = clk_set_rate(dev->mod_clk,
+			   of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun50i-h713") ?
+			   432000000 : variant->mod_rate);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev->dev, "Failed to set clock rate\n");
 
